FracApp MPBrian Arnold, 06/16/97Steven McGrath, 01/01/97Jeroen Schalk, 3-6-95FracApp 3.1 is a fractal drawing program originally written by Keith Rollin & Bo3b Johnson, maintained by Jeroen Schalk for an update to MacApp 3.1 and also added Thread Manager support, courtesy of Tom Becker. Subsequently updated by Steven McGrath for MacApp Release 13 and ACS Threads, highlighting the use of MP threads.A number of compile-time variables control the behavior and speed:qUseAsmComputationIf "1", the 68K version will use an assembly language version of the core computation routine, instead of a C++ method. For PowerPC, this speed up is not used (nor necessary). It is the default for the 68K version. Caveat: it depends on how CFront does its name mangling. If you switch to another C++ compiler, you may get an error during link. Go into GoFigger.a and change the name of "GoFigger__14CFracAppEngineSFRCrT1sT3" to whatever SCpp or another C++ compiler thinks the mangled name should be.qUseThreadsIf "1", the Thread Manager will be used to create thread manager threads to speed up computation even more. The default is to use Threads. If specified, the code will check for the existence of the Thread Manager and the Multiprocessor API Library (MP threads).The 68K version needs to be compiled with FPU support (this is not applicable for the PowerPC version). Also Color Quickdraw is required.Of interest to some people may be the fact that SANE "extended" values are written/read to disk. Note how the PowerPC version uses conversion routines to accomplish this.Status======Compiles and runs on both 68K and PowerPC. Has not been fully tested. Documents can be exchanged between PowerPC and 68K version, even though extended80 (SANE extended) values are written to the document.Notes: For PowerPC you have to link with ThreadsLib and the Multiprocessor API Library.Modification History==================1/1/97:	Updated for MacApp Release 13 using MP and ThreadMgr thread